--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Which files derive from what
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

include/nanoh3/nanoh3.hpp

  Roughly 70% of this file is a statement-order-preserving transcription of
  H3 v4.1.0 C sources into C++, in several places preserving H3's own
  comment wording and magic numbers. The upstream files are:

    src/h3lib/lib/faceijk.c    Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/coordijk.c   Copyright 2016-2018, 2020-2022
                                                Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/h3Index.c    Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/latLng.c     Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/algos.c      Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.

  Original to nano-h3: the Grid<Res> compile-time structure, the face
  Cache and its argmin bound, the exact integer division replacing
  lroundl((3i-j)/7.0L), and cell_fast (a vector gnomonic projection with
  no counterpart upstream).

include/nanoh3/nanoh3_tables.inl

  Data tables derived from H3 v4.1.0:

    src/h3lib/lib/faceijk.c    Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/baseCells.c  Copyright 2016-2020 Uber Technologies, Inc.
    src/h3lib/lib/algos.c      Copyright 2016-2021 Uber Technologies, Inc.

  Eight tables are byte-identical to upstream. Five have upstream's
  symbolic constants replaced by their integer values. Four do not exist
  upstream as tables at all and are a struct-of-arrays decomposition of
  upstream's baseCellData[]. The file's own header comment states this
  per table.

